# Jekyll's Liquid templates. Prettier has no Liquid parser and formats them as HTML, which splits
# a tag across a line break — `{%- endcomment -%}` came back as `{%-\nendcomment -%}`, and the
# Japanese above it ran together into one line. It still RENDERS, which is why it went unnoticed.
# `_layouts/default.html` is the sharper case: it is just-the-docs 0.12.0's own file held with one
# line changed, and its comment asks the next reader to re-align it with upstream on a theme
# upgrade. Being diffable against upstream is the whole point of it, and formatting ends that.
docs/_layouts/
docs/_includes/
